WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.100
For the love of God, what, are they breeding? Good morning Hank, It's Tuesday.

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:06.580
So I'm currently training for a half marathon and a couple days ago,

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:09.900
I ran 12 miles in a row without stopping.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:13.139
I'm not going to lie, I'm extremely pleased with myself, but the point here is that when I am running

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:17.220
I only have one pace, which is the fastest I can go sustainably.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:20.640
Like if I were running from a fast zombie, I could run faster than my running pace,

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:21.930
but only for a few hundred yards.

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:25.680
And then I would stop, realize that my zombie apocalypse strategy is always

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.680
to run face first into the horde of zombies so that I don't have to be, like,

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:30.720
the last person on Earth, and I would give up.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:32.720
Which is not really relevant to the point here.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.440
The point here is that my running pace used to be

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:37.700
about 10 minutes 5 seconds per mile now. It's about 9:40.

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:41.400
I guess I should define what a mile is for people who live outside the United States.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:45.560
So in distance terms, I believe one mile is equal to 22 Kilowatts.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:50.040
Eventually I am going to actually tell the story. So I was running and I wasn't feeling awesome,

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:54.340
and somebody ran past me on the trail, and they gave me a thumbs up.

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:57.900
And I was like oh, God, I hate strangers interacting with me, and there's something vaguely

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:02.160
condescending about a really fit runner giving a schmo like me a thumbs up.

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:04.960
One of the main reasons I like running is that I'm by myself,

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:06.540
and I don't have to interact with people.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:10.580
But after I got the thumbs up a super weird thing happened.

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:13.720
Which is that I started to be able to run faster.

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:16.260
You can actually see this happen on my running app.

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:19.220
You can see the mile where I received the thumbs up.

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:23.140
I receive a thumbs up and then something physiological happened to me

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:24.880
that allowed me to run faster.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:27.940
And also just run more happily, like, suddenly I started noticing the trees

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:30.420
and thinking, *pfft*, it's a beautiful day out here!

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:34.380
What a planet Earth is! Earth really is by far the most underrated planet.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:37.340
So anyway, I was running along and after a wild post-thumbs up,

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:42.299
I started to feel kind of tired again. And then I noticed that someone was running toward me on the trail,

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:44.000
and I thought, do I do it?

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:45.640
Do I dare disturb the universe?

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:48.260
And then as they got close, mostly just to find out if It would work,

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:51.440
I went with the thumbs up, and even though I did not get thumbs back,

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:54.780
I felt the same surge of energy and happiness.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:56.130
And I started running faster,

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:58.060
so the next person that came by, I was like,

00:01:58.060 --> 00:01:58.600
*two thumbs up*

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:00.620
And it continued to work!

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:03.340
Now of course part of me was like, "You have to stop this. This is humiliating."

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:07.740
"You can't throw out thumbs ups everywhere you go, you'll become known as the thumbs up guy."

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:12.420
But then another part of me was like, I just ran the fastest mile of my entire life,

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:15.760
You get a thumbs up! And you get a thumbs up! Everybody gets thumbs ups!

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:18.780
This one we ended off-screen, but it's still there!

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:23.240
It kept working. I have no physiological explanation for this except that it works.

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:26.440
It should tire me out, thumbs it up while I'm running, but it doesn't.

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:27.920
It just makes me feel great!

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:30.160
I absolutely floated through that run,

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:32.820
I mean until about mile 10, then I started to feel terrible.

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:34.600
So friends, if you see me on the trails,

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:36.600
or you see me at a race, don't say anything.

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:37.920
Just shoot me a thumbs up.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:41.280
I absolutely guarantee you that I will return the favor.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:44.320
Okay Hank, I have to go from my last training run now.

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:46.320
I will see you on Friday.

